 text.push_str("\nPrimary B2/32 CPU rises70.210→78.167 ms/query, while maximum lifetime process RSS rises34.25→40.25 MiB versus OFF. At2×2 B2/32 these are76.086→86.364 ms and60.75→67.50 MiB. RSS includes input loading, expected arrays and primes; it is not a full prover peak or minimum RAM. Raw minor faults and context switches remain available. No cause is inferred from fault counts or RAM capacity alone.\n\n## Automatic counters and profiles\n\nAfter all latency,12 FIFO-gated four-event counter panels and12 separate fixed16-million-user-cycle profiles run200 queries after3 excluded primes. Every event reports100% running coverage. These single panels are descriptive, without paired counter confidence intervals.\n\n|Panel|Cycles M/query|Instructions M/query|Cache misses M/query|Branch misses M/query|Samples|\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
