 text.push_str("\nAll28,324 samples have expected PID, registered caller/worker TID, pinned worker CPU, binary MMAP, worker FORK evidence and fixed period; every recording has zero loss, at least1,058 samples and less than1.31% unknown share. B2/32 cycles rise319.864→351.934 million/query versus OFF; instructions rise568.562→570.494 million. At16 workers instructions fall slightly while cycles rise. More leaves and fewer transforms do not establish less CPU service or faster completion.\n\nThe candidate profile has more samples in Window::new and the separate G2 prefix-merge kernel. This is consistent with additional bucket initialization and merges, but symbol samples are affected by inlining and interleaving. The trial does not isolate a cache, synchronization, allocator, clock or dependency cause. Profile shares are not removable wall-time fractions, local CPI or absolute sampling-coverage evidence.\n\n## Qualification and evidence\n\nThe private snapshot has177 files:171 byte-exact originals, five reversible parents and one new child. Independent reverse edits recover all176 original sources. All field source is exact and inherits its qualification. The native run passes128 unfiltered core tests, including48 complete generator-sum cases across1/4 workers, signed/full-width scalar families and lengths1024/1025/4097/8193. Separate ordinary/top bucket oracles cover identities, equal/opposite points and signs. Admission denial preserves words; checked-cost boundaries and overflow are tested. Both raw-image prover tests pass. No fresh field, cubic-feature, portable or complete-proof qualification is claimed.\n\nSource review corrected an unqualified type name before native compilation. An initial analysis-helper link omitted the demangler extern argument and was corrected before capture. Successful native tests, library freeze, final link and complete capture run once; no measured executable or threshold changes during the trial.\n\nAll665 workflow commands complete: four native steps, one final link and660 capture/decode steps. The600 caller processes check18,036 complete query outputs against existing independent full-MSM references. There is no new solve, oracle execution, SDK proof request, Gnark export or verification count. The proof ledger remains27,353. Independent review checks1,298 pin entries, original/private source recovery, actual compiler commands, every raw command/exit/stream receipt, every paired wall/CPU/RSS distribution and gate, all counter values and every profile bin and thread/mapping/loss receipt. No query or proof is rerun by review.\n\nThe candidate is closed as a negative result: repeated transforms were structurally removed, but the combined implementation increased service time and failed latency checks. Its unchanged recipe is not selected for full-proof timing. A next candidate needs a distinct reduction in dominant useful work; adding task parallelism alone has not established the required jump.\n\n## Accepted proof comparisons — inherited, unchanged\n\n");
